Template → consistency
Frontmatter → structured data
Tags → movement & grouping
One folder → mental simplicity
Weekly ritual → maintenance
Checklist → quality control

## 1. Unique ID

* how to achieve this ?


## 2. Status Field (Lifecycle Tracking)

```
status: draft | learning | revised | mastered
```


## 3. Dependency Field (Explicit, not just links)

You already link words. Good.
But links are emotional.
Fields are mechanical.
Example:

```


prerequisites:
  - Uncertainty
  - Sample Space

next:
  - Random Variable

```


## 4.  Revision Date / Versioning

```
last-reviewed: 2026-02-20
```
Memory fades silently.
A weekly ritual without timestamps becomes vague.


## 5. Power / Capability Tagging (Strategic Layer)
You mentioned “what power this word gives.”
Formalize it:

```
gives-power:
  - solve-expectation
  - interpret-probability
```

## 6️⃣ Compression Line (One-Sentence Core)
Inside template:
One-line compression definition.
Because:
If you cannot compress it, you don’t control it.
This becomes exam weapon.

## lean YML

id: CS1-000
module: vocabulary
status: draft        # draft | learning | revised | mastered
prerequisites: [ ]    # list of word titles
next:  [ ]             # logical next words
gives-power: [ ]      # capabilities unlocked
exam-weight: low     # low | medium | high
last-reviewed: 2026-02-22